aker Mike Johnson has campaigned in Bakersfield for Valadao, while outside groups like Giffords PAC are spending against him.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert ratings. Most raters call the race a Lean or Likely Democratic flip, and prediction markets give Valadao only about a 10% chance. Valadao holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, but Villegas benefits from heavy outside spending on his behalf. The race rates as Lean Democratic, with meaningful uncertainty given the absence of polls.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7982, "margin": 5.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8298, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8404, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8532, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8134, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7945, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8475, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8189, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8075, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8433, "margin": 6.2}]}